\tr{\td{The same 230 tests with \code{\verb~|-X engine=machine~} under the launcher's 7 GB machine heap (\code{\verb~|dist-a~})}\td{230 / 230; peak RSS 3.3 GB (\code{\verb~|perf/gf3-matrix-product~})}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rlvm-driver/bin/invariance.sh --no-compile -P 4 published~} - the driver's suite on the published jars: every published test with 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 workers, a session reset after every unit, and pipelined loading with a publication after every unit, every 7 and every 64 units}\td{231 files x 9 runs: 231 correct, 0 wrong, 0 declined, 0 schedule differences, \strong{0 pipelined declines}; PASS}}
\tr{\td{The eight corpora in the default configuration (no option at all)}\td{native image: Init, Std, cedar, reachability, con-leche, navier-stokes-euler, cslib accepted (verdict runs on the efficiency cores); mathlib accepted (\code{\verb~|dist-a~}, window \code{\verb~|t5~}: 92.0 s the first pass, 91.8 s the second, peak RSS 7.2 GiB; and by the arena's procedure on \code{\verb~|dist-c~}, next row); JVM launcher: Init, Std, cedar accepted (window \code{\verb~|b6~}), mathlib accepted with the reference engine (\code{\verb~|dist-a~}, window \code{\verb~|r1b~}: first pass 60.9 s, second 58.0 s, peak RSS 13.0 GiB)}}
\tr{\td{The arena's complete test set by the arena's own procedure (one arena-shaped container, tests one after the other, the arena's time limits, \code{\verb~|perf stat~}; \code{\verb~|work/b2/arena-suite.sh~}, as AR1.md section 1), run line of \src{scripts/arena/rlvm.yaml} with \code{\verb~|--threads 8~}}\td{all tests but mathlib (269; 22:44Z - 22:54Z): good 147 / 147 accepted, bad 92 / 92 rejected, \code{\verb~|either~} 9 accepted / 19 rejected / 2 declined (\code{\verb~|corner-cases/eta-struct-major-no-whnf~}, \code{\verb~|-and-no-whnf~}: the official kernel does not terminate there): \strong{no wrong verdict}, no error, no timeout (closest to its limit: \code{\verb~|perf/app-lam~}, 11.3 s of 70 s); 8.72 T instructions, peak RSS 4.1 GiB; mathlib alone (announced; inside a quiet window, \code{\verb~|am~}, 23:38Z - 23:40Z): accepted in 92.0 s of a limit of 4,120 s, 618 s of CPU, 8,455 G instructions, peak RSS 7.5 GiB. \strong{270 of 270 without a wrong verdict; two \code{\verb~|either~} tests declined}}}
